#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c:12984
msgid "-Error code if validation failed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/amdgpu/display/display-manager.rst:45
msgid "Color Management Properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/amdgpu/display/display-manager:47:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_color.c:40
msgid ""
"We have three types of color management in the AMD display driver. 1. the "
"legacy :c:type:`drm_crtc` DEGAMMA, CTM, and GAMMA properties 2. AMD driver "
"private color management on :c:type:`drm_plane` and :c:type:`drm_crtc` 3. "
"AMD plane color pipeline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/amdgpu/display/display-manager:47:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_color.c:45
msgid ""
"The CRTC properties are the original color management. When they were "
"implemented per-plane color management was not a thing yet. Because of that "
"we could get away with plumbing the DEGAMMA and CTM properties to pre-"
"blending HW functions. This is incompatible with per-plane color management, "
"such as via the AMD private properties or the new drm_plane color pipeline. "
"The only compatible CRTC property with per-plane color management is the "
"GAMMA property as it is applied post-blending."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/amdgpu/display/display-manager:47:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_color.c:54
msgid ""
"The AMD driver private color management properties are only exposed when the "
"kernel is built explicitly with -DAMD_PRIVATE_COLOR. They are temporary "
"building blocks on the path to full-fledged :c:type:`drm_plane` and :c:type:"
"`drm_crtc` color pipelines and lay the driver's groundwork for the color "
"pipelines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/amdgpu/display/display-manager:47:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_color.c:60
msgid ""
"The AMD plane color pipeline describes AMD's :c:type:`drm_colorops` via the :"
"c:type:`drm_plane`'s COLOR_PIPELINE property."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/amdgpu/display/display-manager:47:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_color.c:66
msgid ""
"The DC interface to HW gives us the following color management blocks per "
"pipe (surface):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/amdgpu/display/display-manager:47:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_color.c:69
msgid "Input gamma LUT (de-normalized)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/amdgpu/display/display-manager:47:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_color.c:70
msgid "Input CSC (normalized)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/amdgpu/display/display-manager:47:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_color.c:71
msgid "Surface degamma LUT (normalized)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/amdgpu/display/display-manager:47:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_color.c:72
msgid "Surface CSC (normalized)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/amdgpu/display/display-manager:47:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_color.c:73
msgid "Surface regamma LUT (normalized)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/amdgpu/display/display-manager:47:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_color.c:74
msgid "Output CSC (normalized)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/amdgpu/display/display-manager:47:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_color.c:76
msgid ""
"But these aren't a direct mapping to DRM color properties. The current DRM "
"interface exposes CRTC degamma, CRTC CTM and CRTC regamma while our hardware "
"is essentially giving:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/amdgpu/display/display-manager:47:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_color.c:80
msgid "Plane CTM -> Plane degamma -> Plane CTM -> Plane regamma -> Plane CTM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/amdgpu/display/display-manager:47:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_color.c:82
msgid ""
"The input gamma LUT block isn't really applicable here since it operates on "
"the actual input data itself rather than the HW fp representation. The input "
"and output CSC blocks are technically available to use as part of the DC "
"interface but are typically used internally by DC for conversions between "
"color spaces. These could be blended together with user adjustments in the "
"future but for now these should remain untouched."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/amdgpu/display/display-manager:47:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_color.c:90
msgid ""
"The pipe blending also happens after these blocks so we don't actually "
"support any CRTC props with correct blending with multiple planes - but we "
"can still support CRTC color management properties in DM in most single "
"plane cases correctly with clever management of the DC interface in DM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/amdgpu/display/display-manager:47:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_color.c:96
msgid ""
"As per DRM documentation, blocks should be in hardware bypass when their "
"respective property is set to NULL. A linear DGM/RGM LUT should also "
"considered as putting the respective block into bypass mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/amdgpu/display/display-manager:47:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_color.c:100
msgid ""
"This means that the following configuration is assumed to be the default:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/amdgpu/display/display-manager:47:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_color.c:103
msgid ""
"Plane DGM Bypass -> Plane CTM Bypass -> Plane RGM Bypass -> ... CRTC DGM "
"Bypass -> CRTC CTM Bypass -> CRTC RGM Bypass"
msgstr ""

