#: ../../../gpu/amdgpu/display/display-manager.rst:55
msgid "DC Color Capabilities between DCN generations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/amdgpu/display/display-manager.rst:57
msgid ""
"DRM/KMS framework defines three CRTC color correction properties: degamma, "
"color transformation matrix (CTM) and gamma, and two properties for degamma "
"and gamma LUT sizes. AMD DC programs some of the color correction features "
"pre-blending but DRM/KMS has not per-plane color correction properties."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/amdgpu/display/display-manager.rst:62
msgid ""
"In general, the DRM CRTC color properties are programmed to DC, as follows: "
"CRTC gamma after blending, and CRTC degamma pre-blending. Although CTM is "
"programmed after blending, it is mapped to DPP hw blocks (pre-blending). "
"Other color caps available in the hw is not currently exposed by DRM "
"interface and are bypassed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/amdgpu/display/display-manager:68:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/dc.h:199
msgid "**Color management caps (DPP and MPC)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/amdgpu/display/display-manager:68:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/dc.h:201
msgid ""
"Modules/color calculates various color operations which are translated to "
"abstracted HW. DCE 5-12 had almost no important changes, but starting with "
"DCN1, every new generation comes with fairly major differences in color "
"pipeline. Therefore, we abstract color pipe capabilities so modules/DM can "
"decide mapping to HW block based on logical capabilities."
msgstr ""

